A||||4||Leadfoot||Rear side marker lights||||3||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||06-08-2001||06:14 PM||||I was replacing bulbs the other day and noticed that the rear side marker lights do not flash when you hit the turn signal, but the front ones do.  I opened the the rear side marker cover and pulled out the bulb and it has 2 filaments and not one.  Does this sound right?  Are the rear side marker lights suppose to light when you hit the turn signal?||||reg||3
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||06-08-2001||08:48 PM||||no.<BR>better replace the blub, sounds like it's burnt out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||06-10-2001||06:43 PM||||I replaced all the bulbs with the ones suggested by the owners/sevice manual and it still don't light up when you hit the turn signal.||||reg||9
Z||000003||theogre||06-10-2001||08:54 PM||||That's because rear side markers don't blink... They are just static when the parking lights are on.<P>2 filaments in a side marker... probably not. Those should be those little all glass jobs same as dash backlighting or old style flash bulbs.<P>What makes it look like 2 filiments is probably just a filiment support.<P>Front side markers blink because you can't see the main front turn lamps from a wide enough angle to meet DOT requirements. Just how wide the viewing angle of the main lamps is depends which nose is on the car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leadfoot||06-11-2001||02:53 PM||||Thanks! I was kinda wondering about that, since I only saw two leads going into the light socket.||||reg||1
